  "formContourComment": "Derived from wagner_stereo.wav by pieces/01-wagner/analyze_form.py (lalork repo): RMS + spectral centroid (50/50 blend) -> 48s moving average -> normalize -> histogram-equalize blend 0.35 -> S-curve around MIDPOINT 0.6 with EXPAND 0.55 -> cos^2-crossfaded gain warps -> soft ceiling 0.90 -> centred bin-average to 96 breakpoints. The centroid is blended in because it is terraced where RMS wobbles, and the 48s window nulls the per-chord transient that was spiking the contour on every harmonic boundary (change-rate at boundaries was 1.74x average at the old 4s window). Hand-drawn: 2:00-2:24 small step then relax; 5:12-8:00 extra 96s smoothing + 0.80 trim; 6:00-6:48 forte 0.85; 6:48-7:36 very quiet 0.10; 8:00-8:24 diagonal build to 0.80; 8:48 0.65; 9:12 0.20; building to MAX 1.0 at 10:00, held to 10:20; steep decline to 0.10 by 10:24; tail keeps its analysed shape rescaled. The 10:00 climax is the unique global maximum (next highest 0.895) and is asserted in the script.",
